<title>CANADA: Canada urges swift UN decision on Zaire relief.</title>
<headline>Canada urges swift UN decision on Zaire relief.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Prime Minister Jean Chretien on Tuesday urged the U.N. Security Council to pass a resolution to send a multinational relief force to Zaire &quot;as soon as possible.&quot;</p>
<p>He said the first Canadian troops could be deployed within 48 hours of such a U.N. decision. The first deployment would be a special 350-member Disaster Assistance Response Team (DART), formed by the Canadian military to provide disaster relief at home and abroad.</p>
</text>
